{{Documentation/Header}}
Displays HTML code inline with syntax highlighting, via {{T|inline-code}}. The input is '''parsed''' — use {{T|Htmlir}} instead for markup that must be shown raw.

==Syntax==
{{T|Htmli|v1=html code}}

==Example==
<pre>{{Htmli|<div class="example">}}</pre>

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>1</code> || – || Content || The HTML code to display. || string || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|}

==See also==
* {{T|Htmlir}} — the raw variant, which escapes its input first

<div style="display: none;">
<templatedata>
{
"description": "Displays HTML code inline with syntax highlighting. Input is parsed.",
"params": {
"1": { "label": "Content", "description": "The HTML code to display.", "type": "string", "required": true }
},
"format": "inline"
}
</templatedata>
</div>
